    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="13" relname="preparation">P16 and P22 make good points here about user experience levels.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="3" relname="concession">While P22 correctly states that the HCI community is highly concerned with the range of user experience (i.e., novice to proficient to expert users),</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="16" relname="span">unfortunately, much of the beta testing that goes on is done by proficient and expert users.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="21" relname="span">Most novice users are not involved in usability until after problems are discovered.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="15" relname="span">Part of the problem I see is that our definitions for user experience levels are somewhat simplistic and unmeasurable.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="17" relname="span">The truth is, most of us are novice users in some application and expert on others.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="19" relname="concession">Our "range" of experience matters,</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="19" relname="span">but this is hard to convey on a continuum of user experience levels.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="10" relname="antithesis">We tend to categorize levels,</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="20" relname="span">when the continuum needs more concrete definition.</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="13" relname="span">More research needs to be done in this area, indeed.</segment>
        <group id="12" type="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="span"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="11" relname="solutionhood"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="14" relname="span"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="4" relname="antithesis"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="5" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="18" type="span" parent="6" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="18" relname="span"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="8" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="21" type="span" parent="15" relname="background"/>
    </body>
</rst>
